# Answers for the PCBoard oracle logon (new-user registration path).
#
# Format: REGEX=RESPONSE, first match against the tail of the last read wins,
# so more specific patterns must come first. Rules are matched case-insensitively.
#
# The account is a throwaway fixture that exists only inside the local DOSBox
# image; nothing here is a real credential.

# --- MORE / continue prompts, matched first so they never fall through ---
\(Enter\) to continue=
- more \]-=
More\? \[Y=

# --- identification ---
username:=ORACLE TESTER
apply as a new user=Y

# Once the account exists the board asks for the password directly, so the same
# script drives both a fresh registration and a returning logon.
password:=QX7742ZK

# "Re-enter" must precede the generic password rule.
Re-enter password=QX7742ZK
Password \(one word=QX7742ZK

# --- questionnaire ---
City and State calling from=TESTCITY
Business or data phone=555-0001
Home or voice phone=555-0002
Brand of CPU=PENTIUM
Clear the screen between=N
Default Protocol Desired=N
# An alias collides with the real user base ("User already exists"), so keep none.
Alias Name=
Street \(1 of 2\)=1 TEST ST
Street \(2 of 2\)=
Zip Code=12345
Country=TESTLAND
maiden name=SMITH
gender=M
birthdate=01/01/70
E-mail address=oracle@example.invalid
WEB address=
Set default file description=N
City\?=TESTCITY
State\?=TS
